    },
    "body": "Currently we have no automation in place to check that our code signing certificates are not expired or close to expiry. We have previously \"relied on Release Candidates\" as a dry-run for codesigners to realise that a certificate has expired and have time to fix it.\n\nIn place of this we can run a weekly CI job which will check the certificate's validity and open an issue when it passes an expiry threshold.\n\nIn this draft we only check the windows cert (as I couldn't find a mac one) and we set the alert threshold to 30 days.\n\nWhen the threshold is passed, the job will open an issue in this repo (optionally tagging relevant key-holders).",
